/-!
# A submodule with vanishing geometric stalks over the weak assassin of the ambient module

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S`, let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module and let
`ι : K ⟶ F` be a submodule of it — a monomorphism, with `K` **not** assumed quasi-coherent.
Suppose a set `T` of points of `X` contains every weakly associated point of `F`, and that above
every point of `T` there is a geometric point at which the stalk of `K` vanishes.  Then `K` has
no nonzero section over any étale chart.

Quasi-coherence of `K` is what Stacks 0CU0 — a module with no weakly associated point vanishes —
assumes, and it is needed there: for a module which is merely a subsheaf of a quasi-coherent one
the conclusion fails.  So the hypothesis is not dropped but localised, one section at a time: a
section of `K` over a chart `V` is a *global* section of the restriction of `K` to the algebraic
space `V` presents, and the submodule of `F|_V` generated by such a global section is the image
of a morphism out of the structure sheaf, hence quasi-coherent with no hypothesis on `K`.
Stacks 0CU0 applies to that image, and the stalk hypothesis transports to it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZero_of_forall_exists_subsingleton_geometricModuleStalk`: a
  quasi-coherent submodule whose stalks vanish above a set carrying the weakly associated points
  of the ambient module is zero.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_zero_of_forall_exists_subsingleton_geometricModuleStalk`: **the
  localisation**, that every section of `K` over every étale chart vanishes.

## Implementation notes

The chart space of `V` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSpace`, the algebraic space presented by
the scheme of the chart, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartToSpace` is its étale morphism to `X`.
Its small étale site has a terminal object, the identity chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isTerminalIdEtaleChart`), even though the small étale site of a general
algebraic space does not; that, with
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.sectionsEquivOfTerminal`, is what turns a section over
`V` into a global section.  Restriction of modules along the chart morphism is étale restriction
of sections (Stacks 03LW), so the sections of the restricted module over the identity chart are
the sections of the original module over `V` on the nose.

The geometric point at which the stalk vanishes is prescribed on `X` and has to be moved to the
chart space: that is Stacks 05VN,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_geometricPoint_lift_of_isEtale`, which lifts a geometric point
along an étale morphism over a prescribed point of the source.  The stalk of the restriction at
the lift is the stalk of the module at the original geometric point, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.nontrivial_geometricModuleStalk_etaleModulePullback_iff`.

The instance `Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian`, whose module universe cannot
be the universe of the schemes, is removed in this file: the image of a morphism of modules is
formed here, and the abelian structure that needs is the one of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ModulesAbelian`.

